<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Benavente</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1230</span> · Also known as Treaty of Benavente (1230)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Benavente of 1230 settled the succession of the Kingdom of León after the death of Alfonso IX. His daughters Sancha and Dulce renounced their claims in favour of their half-brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-iii-of-castile">Ferdinand III of Castile</a> in return for pensions. The agreement permanently united the crowns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> and León.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-benavente.jpg" alt="Treaty of Benavente" width="320" height="198" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PMRMaeyaert · CC BY-SA 3.0 es · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monteagudo_de_las_Vicar%C3%ADas,_Castillo_de_la_Raya_Torre_de_Mart%C3%ADn_Gonz%C3%A1lez-PM_17432.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
